From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: explorer: a changed tray icon does not show the old one through it

A notification-area icon window has no background brush and painted its
icon straight over what it showed before: an icon that changed to one with
transparent pixels was blended over the old one (the network icon's
monitor showed through its new Wi-Fi fan). The bar's colour is filled in
first. Gate: make test-trayicon.
---
--- a/programs/explorer/systray.c
+++ b/programs/explorer/systray.c
@@ -178,6 +178,7 @@
     { RGB(0xEE,0xEE,0xEE), RGB(0xF8,0xF8,0xF8), RGB(0xD9,0xD9,0xD9), RGB(0x1A,0x1A,0x1A) };
 static const struct sg_palette *sg_pal = &sg_dark_palette;
 #define SG_COL_BAR      (sg_pal->bar)
+static void sg_fill( HDC hdc, const RECT *rect, COLORREF color );
 #define SG_COL_HOVER    (sg_pal->hover)
 #define SG_COL_ACTIVE   (sg_pal->active)
 #define SG_COL_TEXT     (sg_pal->text)
@@ -642,6 +643,11 @@
         hdc = BeginPaint( hwnd, &ps );
         GetClientRect( hwnd, &rc );
         TRACE( "painting rect %s\n", wine_dbgstr_rect( &rc ) );
+        /* Stained Glass OS: the bar's colour under the icon first. The window
+         * has no background brush, so a changed icon with an alpha channel was
+         * blended over the old one (the network icon's monitor showed
+         * through its new Wi-Fi fan). */
+        sg_fill( hdc, &rc, enable_taskbar ? SG_COL_BAR : GetSysColor( COLOR_WINDOW ) );
         DrawIconEx( hdc, (rc.left + rc.right - cx) / 2, (rc.top + rc.bottom - cy) / 2,
                     icon->image, cx, cy, 0, 0, DI_DEFAULTSIZE | DI_NORMAL );
         EndPaint( hwnd, &ps );
